          "text": "The peak positions are consistent with a primitive monoclinic cell. Three strong harmonic series are particularly diagnostic:\n\n- 22.12, 45.14, 70.29\u00b0 \u2192 002, 004, 006\n- 27.78, 57.37\u00b0 \u2192 200, 400\n- 34.85, 73.58\u00b0 \u2192 020, 040\n\nMixed reflections, especially approximately 202, 121, 204, 411, 420, and 510, determine the monoclinic angle. The resulting indexing is:\n\n\\[\na \\simeq 6.429,\\quad b \\simeq 5.144,\\quad c \\simeq 8.045\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad\n\\beta \\simeq 93.52^\\circ ,\n\\]\n\nwith \\(V\\simeq265.5\\) \u00c5\u00b3 and \\(Z=4\\). The systematic absences favor space group \\(P2_1/n\\), No. 14.\n\nThe lattice and space group are considerably more secure than the light-atom coordinates. Because the pattern contains only a small number of measurable integrated intensities and Li contributes very little to Cu-X-ray scattering, the coordinates below should be treated as a chemically regularized starting model for Rietveld refinement, not as independently determined single-crystal-quality coordinates.\n\n```cif\ndata_LiFeSiO4_primary\n_audit_creation_method\n;Indexed from the supplied Cu Kalpha1 powder pattern.\nThe unit cell and P21/n symmetry are the robust results.\nAtomic coordinates are a prototype-constrained starting model and\nrequire restrained Rietveld or total-scattering refinement.\n;\n\n_chemical_name_common                  'lithium iron orthosilicate'\n_chemical_formula_sum                  'Li Fe Si O4'\n_chemical_formula_structural           'LiFeSiO4'\n_chemical_formula_weight               154.866\n_cell_formula_units_Z                   4\n\n_cell_length_a                         6.429\n_cell_length_b                         5.144\n_cell_length_c                         8.045\n_cell_angle_alpha                      90\n_cell_angle_beta                       93.52\n_cell_angle_gamma                      90\n_cell_volume                           265.5\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn          3.87\n_diffrn_radiation_type                 'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength           1.5406\n\n_space_group_crystal_system            monoclinic\n_space_group_IT_number                 14\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt              'P 1 21/n 1'\n_space_group_name_Hall                 '-P 2yn'\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  '1/2-x,1/2+y,1/2-z'\n3  '-x,-y,-z'\n4  '1/2+x,1/2-y,1/2+z'\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_U_iso_or_equiv\nLi1 Li  0.7490  0.2510  0.2520  1.0  0.025\nFe1 Fe  0.2492  0.2510  0.0065  1.0  0.010\nSi1 Si  0.2515  0.2470  0.4978  1.0  0.010\nO1  O   0.2520  0.0010  0.3480  1.0  0.018\nO2  O   0.4510  0.3970  0.4490  1.0  0.018\nO3  O   0.0510  0.3970  0.4490  1.0  0.018\nO4  O   0.2500  0.4970  0.6480  1.0  0.018\n\nloop_\n_atom_type_symbol\n_atom_type_oxidation_number\nLi  1\nFe  3\nSi  4\nO  -2\n```\n\nRepresentative indexing:\n\n| 2\u03b8 observed | Approx. hkl |\n|---:|:---|\n| 22.12 | 002 |\n| 27.78 | 200 |\n| 34.85 | 020 |\n| 37.06 | 202 |\n| 39.68 | 121 |\n| 41.99 | 022 |\n| 45.14 | 004/220 |\n| 55.41 | 204 |\n| 57.37 | 400 |\n| 62.23 | 411 |\n| 68.91 | 420 |\n| 70.29 | 006 |\n| 73.58 | 040 |\n| 76.38 | 510 |\n| 81.01 | 240 |\n| 83.86 | 431 |\n\nA non-centrosymmetric \\(P2_1\\) model is the principal symmetry alternative, but the supplied powder data do not justify introducing its additional positional parameters. The \\(P2_1/n\\) model is therefore the preferred primary assignment.",
